From 30feccb31f194c3155e2b40e4d4858af3a8ca11d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:21:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 368/368] DOS-PORT: patch 0368 -- lever R3: an unchanged GUI is
 composited once per dirty box that reaches it, not once to their bbox
 (DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP, default on)

Why: with R1 (0366) Maniac Mansion Deluxe in play still drew 78-82% of its ticks on the 486 in the late stretch of
round GC, with the pointer resting on the verb bar (dosags LAB-R3.md sections 0-3). No GUI is re-rendered there:
both 320x57 bottom GUIs are skip-flagged and composited clipped to the BBOX of the dirty boxes and the carry boxes.
That bbox unions the pointer's 16x16 box with Dave at the right fence and three off-camera room objects, so it is
every row from the bar's top to the pointer's bottom at full width: 20,100-32,200 px of masked composite a frame
for a 256 px box. DOSBox-X fixed 40000 (LAB-R3 section 5, fine timing): rb_sprite_time per pass 2.74-4.20 ms on
the bar against 0.69 with the pointer in the room.

What: DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP unset (or any value other than 0, 1, 2) = 4, R3. A flagged entry (0169/0191/0234: unchanged,
same geometry, idempotent) that R1 would clip to the bbox is instead drawn once per dirty box that reaches it:
box[] and carry_box[], each intersected with the entry and the clip in force, a rect inside one already listed
dropped. No box reaches it: skipped (R1's empty-bbox skip runs first as the cheap pre-test). It is R1's exactness
argument with the union of the boxes in place of their bbox: everything written to the buffer before this entry
this frame lies inside box[] U carry_box[], so outside them the buffer still holds this entry's last composite.
Overlapping rects draw a pixel twice, which 0234's idempotence condition allows.
Guards, one per way the restore can repaint more than the boxes say:
 (a) span coarsening: a row that already holds MAX_SPANS_PER_ROW (4) spans takes a further rect by stretching its
     nearest span across a gap (invalidate_rect_on_surf). The stretch stays inside the bbox, not inside a box. It is
     recorded (dos_guiclip_note_span_stretch), latched by the next restore that repaints it (room restore or black
     fill, dos_guiclip_note_restore) and cleared at the end of the composite after it; that frame takes R1's bbox.
 (b) a whole-surface restore the dirty set was not told about: 0366's latch_fullrestore guard, reused unchanged
     (that frame composites every flagged entry in full).
Modes: 4 = R3 (default); 2 = R1 exactly as 0366; 0 = off (every GUI in full); 1 = 0170+0236's clip.
Witness: "DOS-PORT guiclip DOSAGS_GUI_CLIP=(default) mode=4" at startup; guiclip_final in RUNMANI.LOG (both
flavours) gains "boxed= boxes= fb_coarse= fb_whole= span_stretch= coarse_restores=": entries drawn per box, rects
drawn, entries that took guard (a), entries drawn in full under guard (b), stretches, restores that latched (a).

Gates (DOSBox-X, fixed 40000; dosags tests/harness/results/R3LAND-2026-11-06): a per-frame digest of the composited
virtual screen, every tick rendered, default vs 0: EQUAL on every tick of MMD in play (fixture G, 3164 ticks), LAB-R3's
verb-bar fixture V (3964), the MMD intro (1299) and AGS Quest AutoPilot (3558); default vs 2 EQUAL on G and V; a
control that leaves the carry boxes out of the per-box list DIFFs on all four (771-3426 ticks). Each guard forced
in a lab overlay: (a) at most 1 span per row plus a probe pair on a verb-bar row, default EQUAL, guard disabled DIFF
(3002 / 3877 ticks); (b) a whole-surface restore every 7th, default EQUAL, guard disabled DIFF (3002 / 1076 ticks).
Neither guard fired in any unforced run. Release regression vs 0 (5 Days room 3, Trilby room 35, AGS Quest): game
output EQUAL; P9-shape MMD game output EQUAL to the 0367 release. DOSBox-X, fine timing, fixture V: rb_sprite_time
per pass on the bar 2.64-4.10 ms (mode 2) -> 0.73-0.94 (mode 4); pointer in the room 0.586 both.

